   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Family and gender",
     "texto": [
      "In Polish, **mama** and **siostra** are feminine; **tata** and **brat** are masculine. Polish has no articles like «the» or «a»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possessives",
     "texto": [
      "**Mój** goes with a masculine noun: **mój brat**. **Moja** goes with a feminine one: **moja mama**.",
      "**To jest moja rodzina** means «This is my family»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "To have",
     "texto": [
      "**Mam** means «I have» and **masz** means «you have». In **Jak się masz?**, the natural translation is «how are you?».",
      "After **mam**, the noun can change: **brat → brata**, **siostra → siostrę**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
